		{"id":"d986a2cce8503204","type":"group","x":-6000,"y":-300,"width":4200,"height":2960,"color":"1","label":"Docs"},
		{"id":"8f57029626db6776","type":"group","x":-6015,"y":-2100,"width":980,"height":1540,"color":"4","label":"General"},
		{"id":"a47745f0c3fdd179","type":"file","file":"Engine/Architecture - Buckets.md","x":-4960,"y":-240,"width":1600,"height":2920,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"eb5ad60392609a38","type":"file","file":"Engine/StyleGuide.md","x":-5980,"y":-240,"width":1000,"height":720,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"3e8edc694f802701","type":"file","file":"Engine/Glossary.md","x":-3340,"y":-240,"width":1520,"height":2920,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"db9bfd39c0b0bf1b","type":"text","text":"# Rogue Engine:\nIs a role-playing game engine focused on creating content for varying RPG worlds. \n\nThe architecture is a standard mix of non-pure ECS and OOD patterns. What other engines would call a GameObject or BaseEntity, we call an Instance. \n\n- Instances are any engine-defined object loaded in-memory. \n- Definitions are engine-authored content, derived from a DefType.\n- Components are objects of functionality-defining data listed within each Instance. Unlike a \"pure\" Entity Component System, we are not restricting Components to data-only. Functions may be added to a Component.","x":-5995,"y":-2080,"width":940,"height":320,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"7375a20e9117af82","type":"text","text":"## Third-Party Resources:\n\n#### SDL3:\n- SDL_Renderer for 2D graphics.\n- SDL_GPU for 3D graphics.\n- SDL_Window for window handling.\n- SDL_RegisterEvents for basic input handling.\n- SDL_Audio and SDL_Mixer for audio\n#### JSON:\n- Serialization\n#### ImGui:\n- Debug-only UI, and fast prototyping.\n- Release UI will not be ImGui due to limitations in pretty-ness.\n#### Lua:\n- Small-scale scripting, scope is yet to be defined.\n- Bindings will be made manually for now. May upgrade to Sol2 when it can be appreciated more.","x":-5480,"y":-1740,"width":425,"height":720,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"aa9b02b1389f7bff","type":"text","text":"## Engine Buckets:\nSections or \"Buckets\" of code. I.e. when I add something, it most-likely belongs in one of these categories.\n\n#### Def\nDef, DefTable. Tool-side or serialized side of the object model. A def is authored or saved content on-disk.\n#### Sub-record\nSub defining fields inside of a Def.\n#### Instance\nRuntime object model. Runtime root object. Unity's GameObject, Unreal's Actor\n#### Component\nData on an instance, typed by functionality. Ex: HealthComponent, TransformComponent, etc.\n#### State\nSaved fields and data on World. Tracking game progress and character progression. Much of what would be saved mid-game.\n#### Service\nOn-demand cross-object functions. Utility functionality that can reach across varying scopes. Ex: InventoryService::TransferItem().\n#### System\nPer-tick functions that handle the varying 'Systems' of the game. World::Update(), Physics::Update(). Etc.\nCan be registered and expanded upon, similar to CryEngine's registry.","x":-5995,"y":-1740,"width":495,"height":1160,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"8e1e892cd7d30aae","type":"text","text":"## Systems\nSystems.h - Declarations\nSystemRegistery - Register varying systems\n1. CombatSystem\n2. InputSystem\n3. RenderSystem\n4. MovementSystem\n5. PlayerControlSystem.","x":-4980,"y":-2070,"width":380,"height":300},
		{"id":"7c4f3623624dcf73","x":-4580,"y":-2070,"width":460,"height":330,"type":"text","text":"## Components\n1. CombatControllerComponent\n2. HealthComponent\n3. TransformComponent\n4. VelocityComponent"},
		{"id":"55dd1095fb0c24f5","x":-4100,"y":-2070,"width":250,"height":310,"type":"text","text":"## DefTypes:\n1. ActorDef\n2. ArmorDef\n3. ConsumableDef\n4. WeaponDef"}
	],
